            <value>
               <text>Sometimes, filing a proceeding in bankruptcy under title 11 of the United States Code can be a qualifying event. If a  proceeding in bankruptcy is filed with respect to California State University (CSU), and that bankruptcy results in the loss of coverage of any retired employee covered under the Plan, the retired employee will become a qualified beneficiary with  respect to the bankruptcy. The retired employee’s spouse or registered domestic partner, surviving spouse or surviving registered domestic partner, and dependent children will also become qualified beneficiaries if bankruptcy results in the  loss of their coverage under the Plan.</text>
